:: Moving The Pieces [event sister_quest] {"position":"3025,1775","size":"100,100"}
It's evening when I knock on $sister.callName's door. The hallway light is off, and a thin line of warm light leaks out from under her door. Her answer comes out muffled, like she's talking into a pillow, so I take it as a yes.

Her room smells like vanilla body spray and the fruity vape she thinks nobody knows about. Band posters fight for wall space with influencers I couldn't name, and a string of fairy lights loops around her mirror. She's cross-legged on the bed in leggings and a hoodie three sizes too big, phone in hand, and she turns it face down when she sees me. Her eyes are a little puffy. She's done a decent job of hiding it, just not a great one.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
{ who: $sister, text: "If you're here for the charger again, I'm going to start charging rent." },
{ who: $player, text: "Mine's alive, thanks. I actually wanted to ask about the other day. The phone call." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Ugh. You heard that? Great. Perfect. Look, it's nothing, it's school stuff. Don't worry about it." },
{ who: $player, text: "$sister.callName. You don't have to do the whole 'I'm fine' routine with me. I know what drowning in a class feels like." },
{ text: "She gives me a long sideways look, like she's deciding whether I'm worth the effort of a real answer." },
{ who: $sister, text: "...Fine. It's calculus. I used to be good at math. Like, annoyingly good, I never even studied. Now I look at a problem and my brain just leaves the building. And the prof treats every question like a personal insult. I'm pretty sure he hates me." },
{ who: $player, text: "I believe you. For most of high school I was convinced I was just dumb. Math, chemistry, all of it. Everybody else seemed to get it and I was faking my way through. It took me way too long to figure out that half my teachers couldn't explain anything." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Wait, you? You were the smart one. The weird smart one, but still." },
{ who: $player, text: "I was the one who hid it well. I spent a lot of nights thinking something was wrong with me. Then I figured out how to actually focus, cleared my head, and it started to click. I wasn't dumb. I was stuck." },
{ text: "She pulls the sleeves of her hoodie down over her hands and doesn't make a single joke. That alone tells me she's listening." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I keep telling myself it's him. And then I sit down to study and think, okay, but what if it's me?" },
{ who: $player, text: "It's not you. You've always been quick once something clicks. This is a block, that's all. And I might be able to help with that. Remember the demo? I could tune the prototype for focus instead of just calm, and we go through the material together." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You think it'd actually help? Like, make the numbers stop swimming?" },
{ who: $player, text: "You felt what it did last time. Worst case, nothing happens and you've wasted an evening with your favorite $sister.playerRelation." },
{ who: $sister, text: "My only $sister.playerRelation." },
{ who: $player, text: "Still counts." },
{ text: "She chews on her lip, then nods slowly, like she's agreeing to a dare." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay. Fine. Let's try it. But if I still suck at this, you're not allowed to make that face." },
{ who: $player, text: "What face?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "That one. Your 'I'm being very patient' face." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I set the prototype on her desk between a mug of cold tea and a stack of sticky notes and switch it on while she digs her textbook out from under the bed. The settings I pick aren't quite the ones I described. <<UseQuestDevice $sister>>

We start with derivatives, the easy problems first, so she gets a few right before it gets hard. I keep my voice low and slow, and every time she finishes one I lean in to check her work.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
{ who: $sister, text: "Wait. Wait, that actually makes sense. Why does that make sense now?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Because you're not panicking. Do the next one." },
{ text: "She does the next one, and the one after that. Somewhere around the fifth problem she starts tapping her pen against her teeth, which she only does when she's enjoying herself." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay, wow. I think I actually get this. Like, actually actually." },
{ who: $player, text: "Told you." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Don't be smug. ...Okay, you can be a little smug. Thanks, little $sister.callPlayerShort. Seriously." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

By the end of the chapter she's sitting up straight and smiling without trying to. She thanks me twice more on my way out, and neither time is there a joke attached. I switch the prototype off and pocket it. Next time, I think, she'll be the one asking when we can study again.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 10>>
<<NextQuest $sister>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>


